From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:40:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] AROS: event source, waker and terminal queries for AROS
 consoles

Repository: crates.io crossterm 0.28.1 (archive SHA-256 829d955a...dea9c6)
Author: tomaszstaniak
Date: 2026-10-19
Platform scope: target_os = "aros" (x86_64 ABIv11); other targets unchanged.
Upstream status: local-only (not submitted).
Problem: crossterm's Unix backends need mio, signal-hook, rustix and
/dev/tty, none of which exist on AROS (a /dev/tty path even names a
volume and can open a "Please insert volume" requester). AROS has no
SIGWINCH and no select on a console.
Change: an AROS event source. It waits with poll() on the console
descriptor (rust-aros libc answers that with DOS WaitForChar, so an idle
editor costs one request per 250 ms slice), turns on resize reports
(private mode 2048, CSI 48;rows;cols;h;w t, which Limpet sends) and polls
TIOCGWINSZ once per slice until the first report. A lone ESC waits 30 ms.
EventStream works through a flag-based waker. The window size comes from
the console behind stdout, else stdin; the keyboard enhancement query
answers false at once (no AROS console answers it); no tput. Derived from
the isolated mainline candidate in aros-xterm tools/rust-tty.
Verification: host tests (feature aros-event-source) for the parser,
resize reports, escape timing, EOF and waking. On AROS One 1.3 in
Limpet 0.6.0, the experiments/term-probe of the Helix port saw size,
resize, keys, Alt, Ctrl and Esc as sent, and left raw mode cleanly.
Removal: when crossterm gains an AROS backend upstream.
